.TH REPORTMAN-DESIGNER 1 "2026" "Report Manager @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reportman-designer \- Report Manager report designer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reportman-designer
[\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIreport.rep\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reportman-designer
designs Report Manager reports (\fI.rep\fR files): bands, labels, expressions,
charts, barcodes and images bound to database queries. Reports can be
previewed, printed and exported to PDF and other formats.
.PP
When \fIreport.rep\fR is given (a path, relative to the current directory, or
a file:// URI) it is opened at start.
.PP
There are two builds with the same files: the Qt 6 one (package
\fBreportman-designer\fR, recommended) and the GTK2 one (package
\fBreportman-designer-gtk2\fR, transitional). Installing one replaces the
other; \fBreportman-designer \-\-version\fR shows which one is installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and the folders used for translations, samples and
preferences, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage message, then exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Language of the designer, looked up in this order: Spanish, English,
Catalan, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Czech or Lithuanian; any other
language shows the English texts.
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt 6 build only. When it is not set the designer uses X11 (\fBxcb\fR), also
in a Wayland session (through XWayland): with the native Wayland backend
windows cannot be positioned. \fBQT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland\fR runs it on native
Wayland (needs the qt6-wayland package).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/reportman-designer/
Program, translations (reportmanres.*, and languages/ for the LCL texts) and
sample reports (samples/).
.TP
.I ~/.config/reportman/designer_lcl.ini
Designer preferences (window position, last folder). Honours
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.borland/dbxconnections\fR, \fI~/.borland/dbxdrivers
Database connections and drivers shared with the other Report Manager tools.
When they do not exist yet, \fI/usr/local/etc/dbxconnections.conf\fR and
\fI/usr/local/etc/dbxdrivers.conf\fR are copied as system-wide templates.
.TP
.I ~/.repmandlib
Report library connections of the designer.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://reportman.es
